$Module fiftyonedegrees_ipi 4 "51Degrees IP Intelligence VMOD"

DESCRIPTION
===========

51Degrees IP Intelligence module for Varnish.

Load a data file in vcl_init with fiftyonedegrees_ipi.start(datafilepath), then
get the values of properties for an IP address with
fiftyonedegrees_ipi.match(properties).

This module can be loaded on its own, or alongside the fiftyonedegrees module.

$Event init_function

$Function VOID start(PRIV_VCL, STRING filePath)

Return value
	VOID
Description
	Loads the data file. If the file cannot be used, the VCL does not load
	and the reason is reported in the same way as other VCL errors, leaving
	Varnish running the VCL it already had. Each VCL loads its own copy of
	the data.
Example
	::

		fiftyonedegrees_ipi.start("/path/to/51Degrees-IPIV4AsnIpiV41.ipi");

$Function VOID reload(PRIV_VCL, STRING filePath = "")

Return value
	VOID
Description
	Reloads the data using the given data file path, or the original path
	if none is given. If that fails the reason is logged and the data
	already loaded stays in use.

$Function STRING match(PRIV_VCL, STRING properties, [STRING ip])

Return value
	STRING
Description
	Looks up an IP address and returns the values of the properties named,
	in the same order and separated by the delimiter. By default the
	address is client.ip, and the optional second argument gives a single
	IP address to use instead, for example from a header. It does not read
	a list of addresses, so take the address to look up from X-Forwarded-For
	in VCL.

	Each value takes the form "value":weight, where the weight is a number
	between 0 and 1 showing the confidence in the value. A property with
	several values has them separated by a pipe. The double quotes are
	escaped with a backslash, so the string can be used as a header value.

	A property which was not loaded, has no value, or a missing or
	malformed address, gives N/A in place of each value and the reason is
	logged as a VCL_Error record. The request carries on.

	If the values do not fit in the workspace, the result is not set.
Example
	::

		set req.http.x-asn = fiftyonedegrees_ipi.match("AsnName");
		set req.http.x-asn-real = fiftyonedegrees_ipi.match("AsnName", req.http.X-Real-IP);

$Function VOID set_properties(PRIV_VCL, STRING properties)

Description
	Sets the properties to load, as a comma separated list, before start.
	Only loading the properties needed reduces memory use and makes each
	match faster. By default all properties in the data file are loaded.
Example
	::

		fiftyonedegrees_ipi.set_properties("AsnName");

$Function VOID set_delimiter(PRIV_VCL, STRING delimiter)

Description
	Sets the string which separates the values of different properties,
	before start. By default this is a comma.
Example
	::

		fiftyonedegrees_ipi.set_delimiter(";");

$Function VOID set_performance_profile(PRIV_VCL, STRING performanceProfile)

Description
	Sets how much of the data is held in memory, before start. The possible
	profiles are "DEFAULT", "IN_MEMORY", "HIGH_PERFORMANCE", "LOW_MEMORY"
	and "BALANCED". By default the "DEFAULT" profile is used.
Example
	::

		fiftyonedegrees_ipi.set_performance_profile("LOW_MEMORY");

$Function VOID set_max_concurrency(PRIV_VCL, INT concurrency)

Description
	Sets the maximum number of expected concurrent requests, before start.
Example
	::

		fiftyonedegrees_ipi.set_max_concurrency(200);

$Function STRING get_dataset_name(PRIV_VCL)

Description
	Gets the name of the data file loaded.

$Function STRING get_dataset_format(PRIV_VCL)

Description
	Gets the format of the data file loaded.

$Function STRING get_dataset_published_date(PRIV_VCL)

Description
	Gets the date the data file loaded was published, as year-month-day.
